WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.420 --> 00:00:04.940
Hello, and welcome to your second drink of the convention.
大家好，欢迎来到你们大会的第二杯饮品时间。

2
00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:07.640
Ain't no party like a Scranton party.
没有什么派对能比得上斯克兰顿派对。

3
00:00:07.780 --> 00:00:09.140
Because Scranton party don't stop.
因为斯克兰顿派对永不停歇。

4
00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:09.780
That's right.
没错。

5
00:00:10.060 --> 00:00:13.440
So I went back to our mailbag for the convention.
所以我回去翻了翻我们大会的邮件箱。

6
00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:18.840
I looked at comments and mail that we got for after our breakdown came out,
我查看了我们剧集解析发布后收到的评论和邮件，

7
00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:22.060
just to see if there was anything that people felt like we missed.
看看大家是否觉得我们漏掉了什么。

8
00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:23.860
I'm proud to say there was not much.
我很自豪地说，没漏掉多少。

9
00:00:24.260 --> 00:00:28.220
But there was one very big fan mail flurry.
但确实有一大波粉丝来信提到了同一个问题。

10
00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:29.060
Oh, yes.
哦，是的。

11
00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:32.180
And I tried to grab everyone who wrote in about this.
我试着把所有写信提到这件事的人都列出来。

12
00:00:32.420 --> 00:00:33.240
So here we go.
那么，我们开始吧。

13
00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:51.140
Hannah B, Alexis L, Alicia W, Lisa S, Carly D, Susanna W, Jenna D, Taylor R, Nikki W, Jennifer P, Andrew L, Miley W, Haley L, Allie S, Bailey M, Emily W, and Aaron P.
Hannah B, Alexis L, Alicia W, Lisa S, Carly D, Susanna W, Jenna D, Taylor R, Nikki W, Jennifer P, Andrew L, Miley W, Haley L, Allie S, Bailey M, Emily W，还有 Aaron P。

14
00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:52.780
Well, that's a lot of people, lady.
哇，那可是很多人啊，女士。

15
00:00:52.880 --> 00:00:54.280
Why don't you tell everyone what they caught?
你为什么不告诉大家他们发现了什么？

16
00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:56.000
It was a continuity catch.
这是一个关于连续性的发现。

17
00:00:56.260 --> 00:00:58.880
Here's what all those people wrote in to say.
这就是所有这些人写信要说的内容。

18
00:00:58.880 --> 00:01:09.820
That in Season 5, Episode 3, Business Ethics, Meredith admits to having sex in exchange for supplies and Outback Steakhouse gift certificates.
在第五季第三集《商业道德》中，梅雷迪思承认为了换取办公用品和澳拜客牛排馆的礼品卡而发生性关系。

19
00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:10.300
Right.
没错。

20
00:01:10.300 --> 00:01:15.040
And she is having sex with the Scranton Hammermill rep for like six years.
而且她和斯克兰顿的汉默米尔公司代表已经保持这种关系大约六年了。

21
00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:16.540
That's what she says.
她是这么说的。

22
00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:16.880
Oh.
哦。

23
00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:27.620
However, Hammermill was exclusive to Staples until this episode of the convention, which is Season 3, Episode 2.
然而，直到本届大会这一集，也就是第三季第二集之前，汉默米尔公司一直是史泰博的独家供应商。

24
00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:37.040
So by the time we get to Meredith's storyline in Season 5, Hammermill would have only been with us for two years.
所以等到第五季梅雷迪思那条故事线时，汉默米尔和我们合作才不过两年。

25
00:01:37.240 --> 00:01:38.240
It's a lot of math.
这数学算得挺复杂。

26
00:01:38.240 --> 00:01:42.420
And you might think, okay, what happened here?
你可能会想，好吧，这到底是怎么回事？

27
00:01:42.740 --> 00:01:43.140
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

28
00:01:43.340 --> 00:01:55.220
I like to think that Meredith was having sex with the Hammermill rep and that she didn't even know that they didn't supply us with paper until this episode.
我倾向于认为，梅雷迪思当时在和汉默米尔的代表发生关系，而她甚至不知道直到这一集之前他们还没给我们供纸。

29
00:01:55.460 --> 00:01:56.620
I don't know why.
我不知道为什么。

30
00:01:56.780 --> 00:01:58.520
I don't know why I feel like that could track.
我不知道为什么我觉得这说得通。

31
00:01:58.720 --> 00:01:59.640
I feel like that could track.
我觉得这说得通。

32
00:01:59.780 --> 00:02:03.100
I feel like she's probably not really keeping up with where everyone's working.
我觉得她可能根本没在关注每个人都在哪儿工作。

33
00:02:03.100 --> 00:02:08.860
If you say you supply paper to Dunder Mifflin, Meredith will show you a good time.
只要你说你是邓德·米夫林的供纸商，梅雷迪思就会让你度过一段美好时光。

34
00:02:08.980 --> 00:02:09.520
Pretty much.
差不多吧。

35
00:02:09.660 --> 00:02:10.160
There it is.
就是这样。

36
00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:14.220
Well, we also got several letters similar to this one from Meadow S.
好吧，我们还收到了几封类似 Meadow S 发来的信。

37
00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:14.980
Okay.
好的。

38
00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:22.000
In the scene where Michael and Dwight are discussing what possible fluids the black light could be revealing in the hotel room.
在迈克尔和德怀特讨论酒店房间里黑光灯照出的那些液体可能是什么的场景中。

39
00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:22.720
Gross.
真恶心。

40
00:02:23.140 --> 00:02:28.180
Meadow says, I am curious if that was a real hotel room and those fluids were really there.
Meadow 说，我很好奇那是不是真的酒店房间，那些液体是真的存在的吗？

41
00:02:28.340 --> 00:02:31.320
Or did you guys concoct fluids that would show up?
还是你们特意调制了能显影的液体？

42
00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:33.020
If so, what was used?
如果是的话，用的是什么？

43
00:02:33.160 --> 00:02:37.620
I ask this out of a morbid fascination because I fear the fluids in hotel rooMs.
我出于一种病态的好奇心问这个问题，因为我害怕酒店房间里的液体。

44
00:02:37.880 --> 00:02:40.600
So much so that we VRBO whenever possible.
以至于我们尽可能选择 VRBO 民宿。

45
00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:43.640
Assuming and hoping they clean better and wash all the bedding, etc.
假设并希望他们打扫得更干净，清洗了所有床上用品等等。

46
00:02:43.880 --> 00:02:44.500
Thank you so much.
非常感谢。

47
00:02:44.540 --> 00:02:45.700
Love your show and podcaSt.
喜欢你们的节目和播客。

48
00:02:46.040 --> 00:02:46.420
Okay.
好的。

49
00:02:46.760 --> 00:02:47.200
Well.
好吧。

50
00:02:47.460 --> 00:02:49.440
There's no way those fluids were real.
那些液体绝对不可能是真的。

51
00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:49.720
No.
不行。

52
00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:51.500
Please tell me no.
求你别说不行。

53
00:02:51.780 --> 00:02:51.940
Yeah.
是啊。

54
00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:53.240
The answer is no.
答案是不行。

55
00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:53.640
Okay.
好吧。

56
00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:57.060
I reached out to our production designer, Michael Gallenberg.
我联系了我们的美术指导迈克尔·加伦伯格。

57
00:02:57.360 --> 00:02:58.000
Oh my gosh.
天哪。

58
00:02:58.100 --> 00:02:58.620
Poor Michael.
可怜的迈克尔。

59
00:02:58.900 --> 00:02:59.220
I know.
我知道。

60
00:02:59.220 --> 00:03:00.260
What are you texting me about?
你发短信问我什么呢？

61
00:03:00.260 --> 00:03:02.020
What did you spray on the walls?
你在墙上喷了什么？

62
00:03:02.240 --> 00:03:08.560
And he said that he had to reach out to the person he called his quote-unquote paint lord.
他说他必须联系他所谓的“油漆之王”。

63
00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:09.160
Oh.
哦。

64
00:03:09.380 --> 00:03:10.820
Who is Ron Hinson.
也就是罗恩·辛森。

65
00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:12.160
The paint lord.
那位“油漆之王”。

66
00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:12.920
Yes.
没错。

67
00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:17.800
I guess he was in charge of all of our paint for our productions.
我想他负责我们所有制作项目的油漆工作。

68
00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:22.680
He got the tech specs for what Ron used on the walls.
他拿到了罗恩在墙上所用材料的技术规格。

69
00:03:22.920 --> 00:03:28.120
Michael, thank you so much for going to this length for us and our listeners.
迈克尔，非常感谢你为我们和听众们费心去查这些。

70
00:03:28.120 --> 00:03:29.900
Here's what it was.
结果是这样的。

71
00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:33.740
It was a product called Wildfire.
那是一种叫Wildfire的产品。

72
00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:40.140
And evidently, it is only available through film industry vendors, at least at the time.
显然，它只通过电影行业的供应商销售，至少当时是这样。

73
00:03:40.140 --> 00:03:48.460
And it is a liquid reactive medium vehicle that responds to black light but is invisible to the eye in normal light.
它是一种液体反应介质，在黑光灯下会有反应，但在正常光线下肉眼不可见。

74
00:03:49.300 --> 00:03:53.480
Basically, it's just a really high-end black light paint.
简单来说，它就是一种非常高端的黑光漆。

75
00:03:54.120 --> 00:03:54.700
Okay.
好的。

76
00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:57.100
And that is what we splattered all over.
那就是我们到处喷洒的东西。

77
00:03:57.280 --> 00:03:58.140
All over the place.
到处都是。

78
00:03:58.140 --> 00:03:58.460
Mm-hmm.
嗯嗯。

79
00:03:58.720 --> 00:04:03.420
And then he sent me a photo of his view in Florida, and it is gorgeous.
然后他给我发了一张他在佛罗里达看到的风景照，真是太美了。

80
00:04:03.760 --> 00:04:04.060
I know.
我知道。

81
00:04:04.180 --> 00:04:04.980
He moved there.
他搬到那儿去了。

82
00:04:05.120 --> 00:04:05.280
Yeah.
是啊。

83
00:04:05.600 --> 00:04:07.300
I mean, stunning.
我是说，太惊艳了。

84
00:04:07.540 --> 00:04:08.260
He loves it.
他很喜欢那里。

85
00:04:08.500 --> 00:04:09.040
I see why.
我明白为什么。

86
00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:09.660
Will you show me the picture?
能给我看看照片吗？

87
00:04:09.880 --> 00:04:10.380
Yes.
可以。

88
00:04:10.600 --> 00:04:11.240
Look at that.
你看那个。

89
00:04:11.240 --> 00:04:11.940
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

90
00:04:12.040 --> 00:04:12.700
That's lovely.
真漂亮。

91
00:04:12.980 --> 00:04:13.140
Right?
对吧？

92
00:04:13.500 --> 00:04:13.680
Yeah.
是啊。

93
00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:15.220
Thank you, Michael Gallenberg.
谢谢你，迈克尔·加伦伯格。

94
00:04:15.440 --> 00:04:26.460
You know, we also got a fan mail correction from Michael H., who said, in this breakdown, you said the BlackBerry was made by RAM, but it's actually RIM,
你知道吗，我们还收到了一封来自迈克尔·H的粉丝邮件纠错，他说在这次解析中，你说黑莓手机是RAM制造的，但实际上是RIM，

95
00:04:26.680 --> 00:04:29.180
which stands for Research in Motion.
也就是Research in Motion的缩写。

96
00:04:29.580 --> 00:04:32.500
They are a Canadian company out of Waterloo, Ontario.
他们是一家位于安大略省滑铁卢的加拿大公司。

97
00:04:32.620 --> 00:04:35.660
I'm not affiliated with them, but I am a proud Canadian.
我与他们没有关联，但我是一个自豪的加拿大人。

98
00:04:36.420 --> 00:04:39.640
So, given some love to Canada there.
所以，给加拿大点个赞。

99
00:04:40.560 --> 00:04:42.340
Was I the one that got it wrong?
是我说错了吗？

100
00:04:42.520 --> 00:04:43.040
No, it was me.
不，是我说的。

101
00:04:43.460 --> 00:04:43.640
Oh.
哦。

102
00:04:44.260 --> 00:04:44.700
Okay.
好吧。

103
00:04:45.080 --> 00:04:45.220
Yeah.
是啊。

104
00:04:45.400 --> 00:04:46.040
Don't worry.
别担心。

105
00:04:47.560 --> 00:04:50.320
Finally, we got a callback catch from Chris S.
终于，我们收到了来自多伦多的Chris S.的回信。

106
00:04:50.460 --> 00:04:51.020
in Toronto.
来自多伦多。

107
00:04:51.620 --> 00:04:57.860
Chris says, I've been waiting for the convention for so long, ha-ha, but may have missed the boat.
Chris说，我等这集《会议》等了好久了，哈哈，但可能错过了时机。

108
00:04:58.100 --> 00:05:05.380
My fan catch is, Angela, you got such a kick out of Pam storming off and leaving her food in season one.
我的粉丝发现是，Angela，你对第一季里Pam愤然离席并留下食物的片段印象非常深刻。

109
00:05:05.660 --> 00:05:07.520
Which I also loved as an observation.
这也是我非常喜欢的一个观察点。

110
00:05:07.800 --> 00:05:15.240
But it immediately made me think of the convention when you storm off after Meredith says, ugh, that town smells like cheesesteak.
但它立刻让我想到了《会议》这一集，当时Meredith说，呃，那个镇闻起来像芝士牛排，然后你就愤然离席了。

111
00:05:15.420 --> 00:05:20.140
Leaving behind what looks like a bowl of cereal, which Creed promptly begins to eat.
留下了一碗看起来像是麦片的东西，Creed随即就开始吃了。

112
00:05:20.280 --> 00:05:24.520
It's just a small catch, but I've been waiting since season one to write in about it.
这只是一个小发现，但我从第一季就开始等着写信来提这件事了。

113
00:05:24.520 --> 00:05:30.460
All right, Angela, I saw this piece of mail as well, and it made me want to ask you,
好吧，Angela，我也看到了这封邮件，它让我想问你，

114
00:05:30.620 --> 00:05:36.600
in the same way that you have made me re-examine my strong position about Jim and Pam's first kiss.
就像你让我重新审视我对Jim和Pam初吻的坚定立场一样。

115
00:05:36.680 --> 00:05:37.000
Okay.
好的。

116
00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:45.040
Have you reconsidered your judgment of Pam for storming off and leaving part of her meal on the table?
你有没有重新考虑过你对Pam愤然离席并把部分餐点留在桌上的评价？

117
00:05:45.420 --> 00:05:48.200
Here, now your character does it in this episode.
你看，现在你的角色在这一集里也这么做了。

118
00:05:48.800 --> 00:05:54.660
You said you would never in your life leave a half-eaten meal behind if you were in an argument.
你说过如果是在争吵中，你这辈子都不会留下一顿没吃完的饭。

119
00:05:54.820 --> 00:05:57.460
You would at least pick up your things and take them with you.
你至少会收拾好你的东西并带走。

120
00:05:57.600 --> 00:06:00.820
Well, wait, are you asking me the person or Angela Martin the character?
等等，你是在问我本人，还是问Angela Martin这个角色？

121
00:06:01.580 --> 00:06:05.920
I think I'm asking you, the person, because you, the person, judged Pam.
我想我是在问你本人，因为是你本人评价了Pam。

122
00:06:07.960 --> 00:06:08.680
I'm sorry.
抱歉。

123
00:06:08.760 --> 00:06:10.520
I still think I would grab my spoon and go.
我还是觉得我会拿上我的勺子然后离开。

124
00:06:10.760 --> 00:06:12.480
Very tidy, even in an argument.
即使在争吵中也很有条理。

125
00:06:12.860 --> 00:06:14.580
Why would I leave my food?
我为什么要留下我的食物？

126
00:06:14.800 --> 00:06:15.840
It's my food.
那是我的食物。

127
00:06:15.840 --> 00:06:19.780
I might not like the company I'm in, but I'm going to take my food with me.
我可能不喜欢和我在一起的人，但我会把我的食物带走。

128
00:06:19.900 --> 00:06:22.320
This was the same argument you made the first time.
这和你第一次提出的论点是一样的。

129
00:06:23.440 --> 00:06:26.220
And, I mean, it's not unreasonable.
而且，我是说，这并非不合理。

130
00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:28.280
It's not unreasonable.
这并非不合理。

131
00:06:28.760 --> 00:06:29.960
Yeah, I don't know.
是啊，我不知道。

132
00:06:29.960 --> 00:06:34.280
Just because someone's pissing me off doesn't mean they get to, like, have my food.
仅仅因为有人惹我生气，并不意味着他们就能吃我的食物。

133
00:06:34.280 --> 00:06:35.120
I'm taking it.
我要把它带走。

134
00:06:35.280 --> 00:06:36.140
I'm going to eat it.
我要把它吃掉。

135
00:06:36.660 --> 00:06:37.280
All right.
好吧。

136
00:06:37.500 --> 00:06:39.440
Well, thank you, everyone, for writing in.
那么，谢谢大家的来信。

137
00:06:39.580 --> 00:06:41.160
I hope we cleared up a few things.
希望我们澄清了一些事情。

138
00:06:41.160 --> 00:06:43.380
And now, here is the convention.
现在，这就是《会议》这一集。

139
00:06:47.920 --> 00:06:48.860
I'm Jenna Fisher.
我是Jenna Fisher。

140
00:06:49.060 --> 00:06:50.160
And I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是Angela Kinsey。

141
00:06:50.280 --> 00:06:51.420
We were on The Office together.
我们曾一起出演《办公室》。

142
00:06:51.640 --> 00:06:52.680
And we're best friends.
我们是最好的朋友。

143
00:06:52.740 --> 00:06:56.500
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office rewatch podcast just for you.
现在我们正在为你制作终极《办公室》重温播客。

144
00:06:56.660 --> 00:07:01.220
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories
每周，我们都会剖析一集《办公室》，并分享独家幕后故事，

145
00:07:01.220 --> 00:07:03.480
that only two people who were there can tell you.
这些故事只有身临其境的我们两人才能告诉你。

146
00:07:03.860 --> 00:07:04.640
We're The Office ladies.
我们是《办公室》女士。

147
00:07:05.140 --> 00:07:09.190
Hey, Angela Kinsey here.
嘿，我是Angela Kinsey。

148
00:07:09.350 --> 00:07:10.070
It's Jenna.
我是Jenna。

149
00:07:10.350 --> 00:07:12.430
And today, we're talking about the convention.
今天，我们要聊的是《会议》这一集。

150
00:07:12.930 --> 00:07:15.150
It's Season 3, Episode 2.
这是第三季第二集。

151
00:07:15.410 --> 00:07:19.230
Written by Lee Eisenberg and Gene Stepnitsky.
编剧：李·艾森伯格和吉恩·斯蒂普尼茨基。

152
00:07:19.530 --> 00:07:21.570
And directed by Ken Whittingham.
导演：肯·惠廷汉姆。

153
00:07:22.210 --> 00:07:24.290
Jenna, this was a really fun episode for me.
珍娜，这一集对我来说真的很有趣。

154
00:07:24.410 --> 00:07:25.490
I got to travel.
