Angela and Dwight, they're standing on opposite ends of the room.
安吉拉和德怀特，他们站在房间的两端。

631
00:27:24.890 --> 00:27:25.990
They are not looking at each other.
他们没有看对方。

632
00:27:26.150 --> 00:27:32.650
Angela is upset that Dwight is going on this trip because she just really wants to spend time with him.
安吉拉因为德怀特要出差而不高兴，因为她真的很想和他待在一起。

633
00:27:33.370 --> 00:27:35.890
But Dwight is so excited to go on this trip.
但德怀特对这次出差感到非常兴奋。

634
00:27:36.050 --> 00:27:38.710
It's a big deal for him to be included, assistant regional manager.
能被邀请参加，作为助理区域经理，对他来说是件大事。

635
00:27:38.870 --> 00:27:40.730
This is like a big part of his job.
这是他工作中的重要部分。

636
00:27:41.470 --> 00:27:48.410
Angela, it so tickles me how you guys are standing, how you guys aren't looking at each other.
安吉拉，你们站着的方式，你们互不理睬的样子，真的戳中我的笑点了。

637
00:27:49.210 --> 00:27:56.290
Your characters would do this all the time as if people would not be confused by this if they walked in the room.
你们的角色总是这样，好像别人走进房间时不会感到困惑似的。

638
00:27:56.430 --> 00:28:00.830
Now, this is sort of a classic Dwight-Angelo moment within the office that I love so much.
现在，这算是办公室里经典的德怀特与安吉拉时刻，我非常喜欢。

639
00:28:00.830 --> 00:28:02.890
Here's a little interesting tidbit about this.
关于这个有个有趣的小花絮。

640
00:28:03.110 --> 00:28:05.810
And this is on the internet, so you can read about it.
网上有相关内容，你们可以去读一读。

641
00:28:06.050 --> 00:28:09.330
But there was a different scene at the table read.
但在剧本围读时，有一个不同的场景。

642
00:28:09.410 --> 00:28:10.370
I believe it was at the table read.
我相信是在剧本围读的时候。

643
00:28:10.490 --> 00:28:15.150
It didn't make it into the shooting draft where I was upset with Dwight that he was going.
它没有进入最终拍摄剧本，当时我因为德怀特要走而感到不高兴。

644
00:28:15.190 --> 00:28:16.470
So that was the same.
所以这一点是一样的。

645
00:28:16.930 --> 00:28:20.210
And Dwight and I have this exchange in the kitchen where I'm upset with him.
德怀特和我在厨房里有段对话，我对他感到不满。

646
00:28:20.310 --> 00:28:23.510
And then at the very end, I say, I'm late.
然后在最后，我说，我迟到了。

647
00:28:24.310 --> 00:28:26.010
And it's like this cliffhanger.
就像是一个悬念。

648
00:28:26.150 --> 00:28:26.830
I'm late.
我迟到了。

649
00:28:27.310 --> 00:28:28.270
It's like, what?
就像是，什么？

650
00:28:28.470 --> 00:28:29.550
Is she pregnant?
她怀孕了吗？

651
00:28:30.410 --> 00:28:30.810
Yes.
是的。

652
00:28:31.410 --> 00:28:31.810
Okay.
好的。

653
00:28:32.250 --> 00:28:34.270
That did not end up getting shot.
那段最终没拍。

654
00:28:34.490 --> 00:28:35.350
That did not happen.
那件事没发生。

655
00:28:35.570 --> 00:28:40.630
Because I think, Jenna, as soon as we read it out loud, everyone was like, oh.
因为我觉得，珍娜，当我们大声读出来的时候，大家都在想，哦。

656
00:28:40.890 --> 00:28:43.290
And I think Greg was like, wait, this is okay.
而且我觉得格雷格当时想的是，等等，这其实还行。

657
00:28:43.370 --> 00:28:44.270
Maybe this is too soon.
也许这太早了。

658
00:28:44.370 --> 00:28:45.290
This is too soon, right?
这太早了，对吧？

659
00:28:45.470 --> 00:28:46.590
That would have been crazy.
那会很疯狂的。

660
00:28:46.870 --> 00:28:51.270
That would have been crazy if in this episode, Dwight and Angela are already having a baby.
如果这一集里德怀特和安吉拉就已经有了孩子，那会很疯狂。

661
00:28:52.410 --> 00:28:55.870
And, you know, it would have been a weird sort of callback to that time when he asked her
而且，你知道，这会是一种奇怪的呼应，呼应他当时问她

662
00:28:55.870 --> 00:29:00.050
sort of in code if she had any prescriptions, right?
用暗语问她有没有处方药的时候，对吧？

663
00:29:00.430 --> 00:29:01.010
Oh, yeah.
哦，没错。

664
00:29:01.330 --> 00:29:04.690
So anyway, needless to say, they decided to change their minds.
总之，不用说，他们决定改变主意了。

665
00:29:04.890 --> 00:29:05.730
Angela was not late.
安吉拉没有迟到。

666
00:29:05.870 --> 00:29:09.190
She was just upset because she wanted to spend some time with him, which I actually think
她只是心烦，因为她想和他待一会儿，我其实觉得

667
00:29:09.190 --> 00:29:10.150
is really sweet.
这真的很贴心。

668
00:29:10.310 --> 00:29:10.450
Yeah.
是啊。

669
00:29:10.450 --> 00:29:13.330
You sort of get to see the softer side to her.
你算是看到了她温柔的一面。

670
00:29:13.710 --> 00:29:13.850
Yeah.
是啊。

671
00:29:14.050 --> 00:29:18.270
And then I have to bring this up here because so it will make sense.
然后我必须在这里提一下，这样才说得通。

672
00:29:18.430 --> 00:29:24.530
You guys, there are other scenes that we shot that explains how Angela ultimately ends up
伙计们，我们还拍了其他场景来解释安吉拉最终是如何

673
00:29:24.530 --> 00:29:26.310
in the hotel, but they're in the deleted scenes.
出现在酒店的，但那些都在删减片段里。

674
00:29:26.770 --> 00:29:27.250
Yes.
是的。

675
00:29:27.610 --> 00:29:35.690
There's a whole sort of extra plot line here where Dwight secretly gives you a ticket on
这里有一整条额外的剧情线，德怀特偷偷给了你一张

676
00:29:35.690 --> 00:29:37.510
the train to meet him.
去见他的火车票。

677
00:29:37.790 --> 00:29:38.050
Yeah.
是啊。

678
00:29:38.230 --> 00:29:38.730
I know.
我知道。

679
00:29:38.930 --> 00:29:40.830
He gives her that before he leaves.
他在离开前给了她那张票。

680
00:29:40.990 --> 00:29:46.370
But in the break room, I have to just share with you guys this setup of us back to back
但在休息室里，我必须和大家分享一下我们背靠背的场景，

681
00:29:46.370 --> 00:29:49.010
and me at the water cooler and him at the vending machines.
我在饮水机旁，他在自动售货机旁。

682
00:29:49.010 --> 00:29:53.910
We tried a few different positions and this is the one we settled on, but we got so tickled.
我们试了几种不同的姿势，最后选定了这个，但我们当时快笑死了。

683
00:29:53.910 --> 00:29:58.270
We laughed so hard in the scene just at how absurd it was.
我们在那场戏里笑得特别厉害，就因为这太荒谬了。

684
00:29:58.450 --> 00:30:03.870
And then also Ken Whittingham really let us play with how long our pause was until I
而且肯·惠廷汉姆真的让我们自己把握停顿的时间，直到我

685
00:30:03.870 --> 00:30:05.210
said, are you still there?
说，你还在那儿吗？

686
00:30:05.830 --> 00:30:06.010
Yeah.
是啊。

687
00:30:06.210 --> 00:30:12.050
And so there were times where we left a ton of space and we, the longer we didn't say
所以有时候我们留了很长的空白，我们，我们彼此沉默的时间越长，

688
00:30:12.050 --> 00:30:15.410
anything to each other, but stood back to back, the more tickled we got.
但又背靠背站着，我们就越想笑。

689
00:30:16.610 --> 00:30:21.950
And then at the very end, Jenna, I'm curious because I know you have the script, but at the
然后在最后，珍娜，我很好奇，因为我知道你有剧本，但在

690
00:30:21.950 --> 00:30:24.010
very end, I say, don't monkey me.
最后，我说，别耍我。

691
00:30:24.170 --> 00:30:25.590
You can't wait to get out of here.
你迫不及待想离开这儿了。

692
00:30:25.890 --> 00:30:26.590
A-R-M.
A-R-M。

693
00:30:26.910 --> 00:30:30.230
And I, I just like walk out all mad.
然后我，我就气冲冲地走开了。

694
00:30:30.490 --> 00:30:32.930
Now I remember I improvised that.
现在我记得那是即兴发挥的。

695
00:30:33.110 --> 00:30:33.490
Oh yeah.
哦，是吗。

696
00:30:33.570 --> 00:30:34.330
That's not in the script.
剧本里没有那句。

697
00:30:34.630 --> 00:30:39.670
Well, when I rewatched it, I really felt like I heard my accent when I said A-R-M.
嗯，重看的时候，我真的觉得我说A-R-M的时候听出了我的口音。

698
00:30:40.630 --> 00:30:43.550
I think when you improvise, your accent comes out more.
我觉得即兴发挥的时候，你的口音会更明显。

699
00:30:43.810 --> 00:30:44.830
A little bit more.
稍微多一点。

700
00:30:45.030 --> 00:30:45.170
Yeah.
是啊。

701
00:30:45.330 --> 00:30:46.270
So there you have it.
事情就是这样。

702
00:30:46.270 --> 00:30:48.270
That's our little secret break room scene.
这就是我们休息室的小插曲。

703
00:30:48.410 --> 00:30:51.850
And Angela was almost going to have Dwight's baby here.
安吉拉差点就在这儿怀上德怀特的孩子了。

704
00:30:52.310 --> 00:30:52.510
Yeah.
没错。

705
00:30:53.110 --> 00:30:54.550
In an alternate universe.
在平行宇宙里。

706
00:30:55.170 --> 00:30:55.550
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

707
00:30:55.850 --> 00:30:56.090
Okay.
好的。

708
00:30:56.170 --> 00:30:58.670
So now we go to your talking head, Angela.
现在我们来看看你的访谈片段，安吉拉。

709
00:30:59.150 --> 00:30:59.270
Okay.
好的。

710
00:30:59.350 --> 00:31:01.110
And this has one of my favorite lines, Angela.
这里有一句我最喜欢的台词，安吉拉。

711
00:31:01.390 --> 00:31:06.110
You say in the Martin family, we like to say, looks like someone took the slow train
你说在马丁家，我们常说，看起来有人坐了趟慢车

712
00:31:06.110 --> 00:31:06.790
from Philly.
从费城过来。

713
00:31:07.430 --> 00:31:10.570
And you explain that that's code for check out the slut.
然后你解释说那是“快看那个荡妇”的暗语。

714
00:31:11.110 --> 00:31:12.830
Yeah, I am.
没错，我是这么说的。

715
00:31:12.950 --> 00:31:16.030
And then I say, why are there flies in here?
然后我说，这儿怎么会有苍蝇？

716
00:31:16.270 --> 00:31:16.730
Yes.
是的。

717
00:31:17.010 --> 00:31:20.470
We have a fan question from Cody Gold about your talking head.
我们收到一个来自科迪·戈尔德的粉丝提问，关于你的访谈片段。

718
00:31:20.750 --> 00:31:23.850
In Angela's talking head, she swats at a fly.
在安吉拉的访谈片段里，她拍打了一只苍蝇。

719
00:31:24.270 --> 00:31:25.470
Was that scripted?
那是剧本里写的吗？

720
00:31:25.590 --> 00:31:29.870
Or did another bug harass Angela like in the episode, The Fire?
还是说又有虫子骚扰安吉拉了，就像《火灾》那一集一样？

721
00:31:31.090 --> 00:31:35.650
First of all, Cody, we love that you called back the bug from the fire episode.
首先，科迪，我们很喜欢你提到了《火灾》那集的虫子。

722
00:31:35.990 --> 00:31:37.670
Angela, what is the deal?
安吉拉，到底是怎么回事？

723
00:31:38.150 --> 00:31:38.830
I don't know.
我不知道。

724
00:31:38.970 --> 00:31:41.030
I don't know what the deal is with me and flying bugs.
我不知道我和飞虫之间到底是怎么回事。

725
00:31:41.330 --> 00:31:41.770
Seriously.
说真的。

726
00:31:42.090 --> 00:31:44.750
But I was, because I was wondering about this too.
但我当时，因为我也在纳闷这件事。

727
00:31:45.230 --> 00:31:46.870
I have the shooting draft.
我有拍摄剧本。

728
00:31:47.230 --> 00:31:48.930
I didn't see anything about a fly.
我没看到任何关于苍蝇的内容。

729
00:31:49.510 --> 00:31:49.670
All right.
好吧。

730
00:31:49.810 --> 00:31:53.950
So Jenna, do you remember when we were filming this episode, it was insanely hot.
珍娜，你还记得我们拍这一集的时候吗，当时热得要命。

731
00:31:54.090 --> 00:31:55.590
There was this crazy heat wave.
有一场疯狂的热浪。

732
00:31:55.590 --> 00:31:56.450
It was in AuguSt.
那是在八月。

733
00:31:57.210 --> 00:32:00.170
And as a result, there were all of these like flies.
结果就是，到处都是这种苍蝇。

734
00:32:00.250 --> 00:32:01.890
I don't know if you remember this.
不知道你还记不记得。

735
00:32:02.190 --> 00:32:02.530
Oh yeah.
哦，记得。

736
00:32:02.530 --> 00:32:04.330
It was like a fly infestation.
简直是苍蝇泛滥。

737
00:32:04.490 --> 00:32:07.070
I think they were coming in to get out of the heat.
我觉得它们是想进来避暑。

738
00:32:07.270 --> 00:32:08.190
I think they were too.
我也觉得是。

739
00:32:08.190 --> 00:32:09.390
I think we'd open the doors.
我想我们当时打开了门。

740
00:32:09.650 --> 00:32:11.370
The flies were like, it's super hot out.
苍蝇们心想，外面太热了。

741
00:32:11.630 --> 00:32:11.790
Yeah.
没错。

742
00:32:11.870 --> 00:32:13.330
The flies were like, oh, air conditioning.
苍蝇们心想，哦，有空调。

743
00:32:13.550 --> 00:32:14.330
I'm getting in there.
我要钻进去。

744
00:32:14.510 --> 00:32:17.870
So this talking head, we filmed it right after lunch that day.
所以这个访谈片段，我们那天午饭后马上就拍了。

745
00:32:18.170 --> 00:32:21.610
And you know, whenever we would have lunch, Jenna, they would leave the doors open longer.
你知道，每次我们吃午饭时，珍娜，他们都会把门开得久一点。

746
00:32:21.810 --> 00:32:22.210
Yeah.
没错。

747
00:32:22.630 --> 00:32:23.910
To kind of air it out.
为了通通风。

748
00:32:24.050 --> 00:32:28.450
And there were like five or six of these dudes buzzing around my head the whole time
在我做这个访谈的时候，有五六只这种家伙一直在我的头顶嗡嗡乱飞。

749
00:32:28.450 --> 00:32:30.190
I was doing this talking head.
我当时正在录制。

750
00:32:30.190 --> 00:32:36.250
So one time I just swatted at one while staying in character and Gene, our writer was in the
所以有一次我保持着角色状态顺手拍死了一只，而我们的编剧吉恩当时就在

751
00:32:36.250 --> 00:32:37.970
room with me and that cracked him up.
和我待在一个房间里，这让他笑坏了。

752
00:32:38.110 --> 00:32:38.910
He loved it.
他很喜欢。

753
00:32:39.070 --> 00:32:42.410
And he was like, Ange, will you, will you swat at flies again?
然后他说，安吉，你能不能再拍一次苍蝇？

754
00:32:42.670 --> 00:32:43.730
And I was like, okay.
我说，好吧。

755
00:32:43.910 --> 00:32:46.870
So I did it again, but this time I ad-libbed the line.
于是我又拍了一次，但这次我即兴加了一句台词。

756
00:32:47.030 --> 00:32:48.190
Why are there flies in here?
为什么这里会有苍蝇？

757
00:32:48.350 --> 00:32:52.490
And then we did another take and I swatted more and I ad-libbed that, you know what?
然后我们又拍了一遍，我拍得更起劲了，我还即兴说了句，你知道吗？

758
00:32:52.610 --> 00:32:53.670
This is all Kevin's fault.
这全怪凯文。

759
00:32:54.030 --> 00:32:55.490
He had smelly takeout.
他带了味道很大的外卖。

760
00:32:55.490 --> 00:33:00.210
And I did this whole really mean riff on Kevin's food that attracted the flies.
然后我针对凯文引来苍蝇的食物进行了一番刻薄的吐槽。

761
00:33:00.490 --> 00:33:03.770
That did not make it in, but my other improv line did.
那段没被剪进正片，但我即兴加的另一句台词进去了。

762
00:33:03.990 --> 00:33:04.610
Oh my God.
天哪。

763
00:33:04.610 --> 00:33:05.350
That is amazing.
太棒了。

764
00:33:05.470 --> 00:33:07.570
But here's the thing, Angela, I'll have you know,
但重点是，安吉拉，我得告诉你，

765
00:33:08.450 --> 00:33:13.030
none of your talking head that is in the script is the same as the episode.
你那段访谈里没有一句台词是剧本里原本写的。

766
00:33:13.190 --> 00:33:13.910
I looked it up.
我查过了。

767
00:33:14.150 --> 00:33:16.630
Wait, so the slow train from Philly isn't in the script?
等等，所以“费城慢车”那句不在剧本里？

768
00:33:16.890 --> 00:33:18.470
Slow train from Philly is not in the script either.
“费城慢车”也不在剧本里。

769
00:33:18.670 --> 00:33:19.570
Fly is not in the script.
苍蝇那段也不在剧本里。

770
00:33:19.730 --> 00:33:21.230
Slow train from Philly, not in the script.
“费城慢车”，不在剧本里。

771
00:33:21.490 --> 00:33:24.270
Here is what your talking head was supposed to be.
这是你原本应该说的访谈台词。

772
00:33:24.270 --> 00:33:25.210
Oh my gosh.
天哪。

773
00:33:25.370 --> 00:33:25.490
Yeah.
是啊。

774
00:33:25.590 --> 00:33:26.350
Here, I want to hear it.
来，我想听听。

775
00:33:26.470 --> 00:33:27.110
Here it is.
给你。

776
00:33:27.710 --> 00:33:28.150
Yes.
好。

777
00:33:28.370 --> 00:33:31.530
Michael and Dwight Schrute are going to a convention in Philadelphia.
迈克尔和德怀特·舒鲁特要去费城参加一个大会。

778
00:33:31.810 --> 00:33:35.010
Personally, I find even the idea of a convention repulsive.
个人而言，我甚至觉得“大会”这个概念就很令人反感。

779
00:33:35.370 --> 00:33:38.690
All those people from different places gathered together,
所有那些来自不同地方的人聚在一起，

780
00:33:38.930 --> 00:33:41.010
breathing hot breath all over each other.
对着彼此呼出热气。

781
00:33:41.150 --> 00:33:41.930
It's disgusting.
太恶心了。

782
00:33:42.930 --> 00:33:45.890
Did you like my attempt to read it as Angela Martin?
我模仿安吉拉·马丁的语气读得怎么样？

783
00:33:46.130 --> 00:33:47.050
I loved it.
我很喜欢。

784
00:33:47.150 --> 00:33:47.650
I loved it.
我太喜欢了。

785
00:33:47.730 --> 00:33:49.230
I remember when we were doing this talking head,
我记得我们拍这段访谈的时候，

786
00:33:49.350 --> 00:33:51.810
